# L §5.19 One movement on two statements: rows stated same are one movement, "counted once by observed(m[k]) and
# flows" (L §6.1: "counted once by flows and observed"). One transfer of 950.00 from konto to sav on both
# statements, each row fulfilling save[2026-03], the second statement stating them same: flows of save and
# observed(save[2026-03]) count it once, as the binding and the balances do (M2 patch case P35; refcore counted it
# twice, 1 900.00). save is a decision dated the rows' day.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-03-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
input bank: observed
input keep: money PLN
input d_save: int

move save[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, d_save)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

ask q_save: flows(save, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31)
ask q_obs: observed(save[2026-03]).cash.amount
ask q_moved: sum(t.cash.amount for t in transfers over 2026-03)
ask q_sav: bal(sav, 2026-03-31)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d_save = 15 "s"
  opening[konto] = 1050.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st_konto
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto
  bank[a2] = (on: 2026-03-15, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 950.00 PLN, fulfils: save[2026-03]) "a"

version st_sav
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-03
  covers sav
  bank[b1] = (on: 2026-03-15, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 950.00 PLN, fulfils: save[2026-03]) "b"
  same bank[a2] = bank[b1]
=== expect
q_moved: 950.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
q_obs: 950.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
q_sav: 950.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
q_save: 950.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
